{"name":"Eight Ball","hex":"#03050a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"eight ball","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of eight-ball."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eight_ball"}],"entries":[{"title":"Eight Ball (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Eight Ball is a 1992 Australian film co-written and directed by Ray Argall."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight_Ball_(film)"},{"title":"Eight-ball","blocks":[{"text":"Eight-ball is a discipline of pool played on a billiard table with six pockets, cue sticks, and sixteen billiard balls. The object balls include seven solid-colored balls numbered 1 through 7, seven striped balls numbered 9 through 15, and the black 8 ball. After the balls are scattered with a break shot, a player is assigned either the group of solid or striped balls once they have legally pocketed a ball from that group. The object of the game is to legally pocket the 8-ball in a \"called\" pocket, which can only be done after all of the balls from a player's assigned group have been cleared from the table."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Eight_Ball_Rack_2005_SeanMcClean.jpg/330px-Eight_Ball_Rack_2005_SeanMcClean.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eight-ball"},{"title":"8","blocks":[{"text":"8 (eight) is the natural number following 7 and preceding 9."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8"},{"title":"Ball","blocks":[{"text":"A ball is a round object. Balls can have several uses. For example they are used in ball games, where the play of the game follows the state of the ball as it is hit, kicked or thrown by players. Balls can also be used for simpler activities, such as catch or juggling. Balls made from hard-wearing materials are used in engineering applications to provide very low friction bearings, known as ball bearings. Black-powder weapons use stone and metal balls as projectiles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Many_balls.jpg/330px-Many_balls.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ball"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/8_ball_break_time_lapse.jpg/500px-8_ball_break_time_lapse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/8_ball_break_time_lapse.jpg/500px-8_ball_break_time_lapse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Long-exposure photograph of a break in eight-ball","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A8_ball_break_time_lapse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/8-Ball.jpg/500px-8-Ball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ab/8-Ball.jpg/500px-8-Ball.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An 8-ball in pool","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A8-Ball.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg/500px-Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg/1280px-Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg/500px-Balls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABalls_-_10-15c_-_Novgorod_Kremlin_Museum.jpg"},{"srcse